WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.772
Not every hunt discovers active attackers, and that is acceptable.

2
00:00:03.772 --> 00:00:16.353
A successful hunt may uncover malicious activity, validate that a concern does not currently appear present, identify visibility gaps, improve documentation, or refine future hypotheses.

3
00:00:16.353 --> 00:00:18.808
Negative findings can still provide value.

4
00:00:18.808 --> 00:00:27.000
If the hunt was well scoped and the data was strong, the team may gain confidence that a specific behavior was not observed during the period reviewed.

5
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:36.878
Findings from hunts can become SIEM correlation rules, EDR detections, playbooks, dashboards, enrichment logic, and analyst training materials.

6
00:00:36.878 --> 00:00:40.510
Hunting turns investigative learning into operational improvement.

7
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:46.855
Over time, threat hunting strengthens the organization's ability to detect and respond to future attacks.

8
00:00:46.855 --> 00:00:52.722
It helps security teams learn from their own environment instead of relying only on generic assumptions.
